-- title:
--   Multiplication by p from level w+1 to level w
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring, $p$ a prime, $h$ a natural number and $G$ a $p$-divisible group over $R$ of height $h$ in the sense of the project structure: a family of commutative rings $G.\mathrm{level}\,v$, each a cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebra that is finite and free as an $R$-module, with surjective $R$-bialgebra maps $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v : G.\mathrm{level}(v+1) \to G.\mathrm{level}\,v$, with $\operatorname{rank}_R G.\mathrm{level}\,v = p^{vh}$, and with the kernel of $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v$ equal to the image of the augmentation ideal (the kernel of the counit) of $G.\mathrm{level}(v+1)$ under the $p^v$-th convolution power `nsmulAlgHom` of the identity. Let $w$ be a natural number. Then there is an $R$-bialgebra map $m : G.\mathrm{level}\,w \to G.\mathrm{level}(w+1)$ such that: the composite of $G.\mathrm{transition}\,w$ followed by $m$ equals `nsmulAlgHom R (G.level (w+1)) p`; the composite of $m$ followed by $G.\mathrm{transition}\,w$ equals `nsmulAlgHom R (G.level w) p`; $m$ is injective; the ideal of $G.\mathrm{level}(w+1)$ generated by the image under $m$ of the augmentation ideal of $G.\mathrm{level}\,w$ equals the image of the augmentation ideal of $G.\mathrm{level}(w+1)$ under `nsmulAlgHom R (G.level (w+1)) p`; and, with respect to the $G.\mathrm{level}\,w$-algebra structure on $G.\mathrm{level}(w+1)$ given by $m$, the ring $G.\mathrm{level}(w+1)$ is faithfully flat over $G.\mathrm{level}\,w$.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic form of Tate's statement that multiplication by $p$ induces an epimorphism $G_{w+1} \to G_w$ of $p$-divisible groups whose kernel is the level-one piece, together with the faithful flatness of such a quotient map. It is used in the analysis of when a transition map kills an element, via membership in the torsion ideal attached to the Hopf-algebra kernel.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_exists_bialgHom_comp_transition_eq_nsmulBialgHom_and_injective_and_map_ker_counit_eq_torsionIdeal_and_faithfullyFlat.lean

